---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/layout/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/layout/Footer.astro';
import Container from '../components/ui/Container.astro';
import Section from '../components/ui/Section.astro';
import Badge from '../components/ui/Badge.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy" description="How Continuum Dataguard Technologies handles personal information collected through this website and the Neptune app.">
  <Header slot="header" />

  <Section>
    <Container class="max-w-3xl">
      <Badge>Privacy Policy</Badge>
      <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl text-paper">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-mist">
        This Privacy Policy explains how Continuum Dataguard Technologies ("Continuum", "we",
        "us") handles personal information in connection with this website and the Neptune
        mobile app, which Continuum develops and operates.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-12 flex flex-col gap-10">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-paper">Introduction</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-mist">
            This policy applies to the Continuum Dataguard Technologies website and to the
            Neptune app. It explains what personal information may be collected, how it is
            used, and the choices available to you.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-paper">Information collected through this website</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-mist">
            The website's contact form asks for your name, email address, organisation (optional)
            and the content of your message. This information is only collected if you choose to
            submit it. Browsing the website itself does not require an account.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-paper">Information collected through the Neptune app</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-mist">
            Using the Neptune app requires an account. The app collects the following categories
            of information:
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg text-paper">Account information</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-mist">
            Your email address and password when you create an account. Your password is handled
            by our authentication provider and stored using industry-standard security practices;
            Continuum does not have access to your password in readable form.
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg text-paper">Location and GPS data</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-mist">
            When you use a location-based feature (such as viewing nearby fishing spots, or
            checking marine and weather conditions for your area), Neptune will ask for
            permission to access your device's location while the app is in use. Neptune does
            not access your location in the background or when the app is closed. Your
            coordinates are used to request weather, marine and tide information for that
            location, as described further under "Cloud services and third-party services"
            below. Your precise coordinates are not saved as part of your catch or fishing
            session records — those records store a location description rather than raw GPS
            coordinates.
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg text-paper">Catch and fishing session records</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-mist">
            When you log a catch or a fishing session, Neptune stores the information you enter —
            such as species, date and time, a location description, weight and length (where
            provided), bait, hook, trace and notes — together with, where available, a
            snapshot of weather and marine conditions (such as wind, swell, tide and moon phase)
            recorded automatically at that time to help you review conditions later.
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg text-paper">Digital Fishing Licence Vault</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-mist">
            If you choose to use the Digital Fishing Licence Vault, Neptune stores a copy of your
            licence document together with details such as your name, licence number, issuing
            authority and validity dates, entirely on your own device. This information is not
            uploaded to Supabase or any other Continuum server, and Continuum cannot access it.
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg text-paper">Account status</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-mist">
            Your account record includes a status indicating whether you have Free or Premium
            access. Premium pricing and features are still being finalised and are not yet
            available for purchase through the app.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-paper">How information is used</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-mist">
            Information submitted through the website's contact form is used solely to respond
            to your enquiry. Information collected through the Neptune app is used to provide
            your account and the features you use — including storing your catch and fishing
            session records for your own reference, providing weather, marine and tide
            information, maintaining your Free/Premium account status, and diagnosing and fixing
            technical problems. We do not use this information for advertising, or for any
            purpose unrelated to providing and supporting the website or the app.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-paper">Contact enquiries</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-mist">
            When you submit the contact form, the details you provide are used to understand and
            respond to your enquiry. We do not share the contents of your enquiry other than as
            necessary to respond to it or as required by law.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-paper">Cloud services and third-party services</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-mist">
            Neptune's account, catch, fishing session and account-status data is stored using
            Supabase, our backend and database provider. This project's Supabase infrastructure
            is hosted in the eu-west-1 (Ireland) region.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-mist">
            To provide weather and marine condition information, Neptune sends your device's
            coordinates directly to Open-Meteo, a third-party weather data provider, when you
            request that information for your location. To provide tide information, Neptune
            sends an approximate, rounded version of your coordinates to our own backend, which
            requests tide data from WorldTides on your behalf — WorldTides does not receive your
            exact location directly from your device.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-mist">
            Neptune uses Firebase Crashlytics, a Google service, to help us identify and fix
            technical problems. If the published app encounters an error, technical diagnostic
            information (such as device type, operating system version, and details about the
            error) may be sent to Firebase. This only applies to the published app, not to
            development or testing builds.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-paper">Website and technical information</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-mist">
            As with most websites, our hosting infrastructure may automatically process standard
            technical information — such as IP address, browser type and access times — as part
            of normal website operation. This information is not used to personally identify
            visitors.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-paper">Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-mist">
            This website does not currently use cookies or similar tracking technologies. The
            Neptune app does not use advertising or analytics tracking technologies. If this
            changes in future, this policy will be updated accordingly.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-paper">Disclosure of information</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-mist">
            We do not sell or trade personal information. Information is disclosed only to the
            service providers described above (necessary to operate the website and the app), or
            where disclosure is required by law.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-paper">Data security</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-mist">
            We take reasonable measures to protect personal information against loss, misuse and
            unauthorised access, appropriate to the nature of the information involved. Your
            catch and fishing session records are stored in a way that restricts access to your
            own account — other Neptune users cannot view your records.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-paper">Data retention</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-mist">
            Personal information submitted through the website's contact form is retained only
            for as long as is reasonably necessary to respond to your enquiry, after which it
            may be securely deleted.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-mist">
            There is currently no fixed automatic retention period for Neptune app account,
            catch or fishing-session data. This data is kept until you delete an individual
            record, or until you delete your account as described below.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-paper">Account and data deletion</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-mist">
            You can delete an individual catch record at any time from within the app. You can
            also permanently delete your entire Neptune account from the app's Profile screen.
            Account deletion is immediate once confirmed and cannot be undone. Deleting your
            account removes your catch records, your fishing session records, your account
            status information, and your authentication/account data.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-mist">
            The Digital Fishing Licence Vault is stored only on your own device and is not
            uploaded to Supabase, so it is not removed by server-side account deletion. If you
            want to remove that information as well, you can delete it directly within the app,
            or by uninstalling the app from your device.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-paper">Your rights under South African law</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-mist">
            South Africa's Protection of Personal Information Act (POPIA) gives individuals
            rights in relation to their personal information, including the right to request
            access to, correction of, or deletion of personal information held about them, and
            the right to lodge a complaint with the Information Regulator. Requests relating to
            personal information collected through the website or the Neptune app can be
            directed to Continuum using the contact details below.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-paper">International data location</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-mist">
            The infrastructure Continuum uses to operate the Neptune app, including Supabase and
            Firebase, may store and process information outside South Africa. Using the website
            or the app may therefore involve your information being processed internationally.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-paper">Children's privacy</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-mist">
            The website and the Neptune app are not directed at children, and we do not
            knowingly collect personal information from children.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-paper">Contact us about this policy</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-mist">
            Questions or requests regarding personal information can be directed to:
          </p>
          <div class="mt-4 flex flex-col gap-2">
            <p class="font-mono text-sm text-paper">Continuum Dataguard Technologies</p>
            <p class="font-mono text-sm text-mist">Durban, KwaZulu-Natal, South Africa</p>
            <a href="mailto:continuumdataguardtech@outlook.com" class="font-mono text-sm text-paper hover:text-signal">
              continuumdataguardtech@outlook.com
            </a>
            <a href="https://wa.me/27611519561" class="font-mono text-sm text-paper hover:text-signal">
              WhatsApp: +27 61 151 9561
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-paper">Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-mist">
            This policy may be updated from time to time to reflect changes to the website, the
            Neptune app, or applicable law. Any changes will be posted on this page.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</Layout>
